{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 16, :comments ["<b>And Elohim made, etc.</b> The reason He was not satisfied with what He had already said — ״וַיְהִי כֵן״ — concerning all that was mentioned, is that this is a new act. For after the moon was diminished, as stated in the words of the Sages, HaShem remedied and established a new act: He established dominion for the moon at night, for by day it has no dominion before the light of the sun, and He assigned it the stars. And there is no contradiction in this to what HaShem said at the beginning of His words, for He already hinted at the ultimate outcome from its very beginning, as I examined in His saying ״יְהִי.״ And although we explained that in a different manner, it bears both interpretations."], :book :genesis, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T18:55:59.347660954Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}